.TH LUNISOLAR 1.SH NAMElunisolar \- the phase of the moon, or a lunisolar calendar.SH SYNOPSIS\fBlunisolar\fR.br\fBlunisolar\fRyear zone.SH DESCRIPTIONWith no arguments,\fBlunisolar\fRprints the moon's phase now in one line:.nf    The moon is waxing and gibbous (79% of full)..fiGiven a year and a time zone it writes, instead, a LaTeX document ofthat year's lunisolar calendar: each season drawn as a circle of dates,with the new and full moons on it.  Run the output through\fBlatex\fRto typeset it.  The zone is one of\fBGMT\fR,\fR\fBBST\fR,\fR\fBNST\fR,\fR\fBAST\fR,\fR\fBEST\fR,\fR\fBCST\fR,\fR\fBMST\fR,\fR\fBPST\fR,\fR\fBYST\fR,\fR\fBHST\fRor\fBJST\fR.\fR.SH EXAMPLES.nflunisolarlunisolar 1995 GMT > luna.tex.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOphoon, latex